-- title:
--   Stability of the Gauss ring under a level automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')` on $(\mathbb{Z}/q^{2}M')^{\times}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, and let $W_0\subseteq K$ be the valuation subring consisting of those $f$ for which $f\cdot y=x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ for some power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ non-zero modulo the maximal ideal (the Gauss ring). Assume given automorphisms $\tau(\gamma)\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ such that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M') γ⁻¹`, i.e. for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_H(q^{2}M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\ne 0$, and every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is $p_f/p_g$, applying any embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$ to $\tau(\gamma)x$ and multiplying by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ gives the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$. Fix further: a ring homomorphism $e:L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; a valuation subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A'$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\zeta'=e\zeta$; a ring homomorphism $\iota_K$ from $K$ to `fieldBar q M'` acting on Laurent series by applying $e$ to coefficients; the Gauss ring $O$ of `fieldBar q M'` relative to $A'$, defined by $f\in O$ iff $f\cdot y=x$ for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A'$ with $y$ non-zero modulo the maximal ideal; the compatibility $\iota_K f\in O\iff f\in W_0$; and the intertwining property that for $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0(M')$ every $\sigma\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M') ε K σ` satisfies $\iota_K\circ\sigma=\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\varepsilon\circ\iota_K$. Then, for $\varphi\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ and $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\iota_K\circ\varphi=\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\varepsilon\circ\iota_K$, the pullback of $W_0$ along $\varphi$ equals $W_0$ if and only if the reduction `redQ q ε` of $\varepsilon$ in $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ fixes the point $[1:0]$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$.
--
--   This is the elementwise form of the statement that, among the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, exactly those whose reduction modulo $q$ lies in the Borel stabiliser of the line $[1:0]$ preserve the Gauss valuation ring, i.e. the branch at infinity of the Igusa-type degeneration of $X_H(q^2M')$ in characteristic $q$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_gauss_eq_comap_gauss_iff_redQ_inv_smul_lineInfty_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_isAlgebraic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_gauss_eq_comap_gauss_iff_redQ_inv_smul_lineInfty_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_isAlgebraic), which recasts the criterion as a comparison of two pulled-back valuation rings.
